 "power_notes": "Track widths here are sized for the tracks that remain: plane taps and short stubs. The main currents ride on copper the width rules can't see: VBUS_IN/VBUS/PVDD/+3V3 on In2 plane regions plus F.Cu pours, and the amp OUT/SPK nets (3.7 A rms continuous sine, 2 x 56 W governor-capped) on the solid fan-in pours from kicad/gen/power_zones.py. check_irdrop covers those paths at P8.",
 "diff_pairs_note": "Explicitly empty. The USB full-speed pair (12 Mb/s) and the two 100BASE-TX pairs run about 10 mm, so coupling them adds nothing measurable, and the router doesn't couple pairs (route_critical's KRT diff pass shorted). They are routed as ordinary nets at the Default width."
